  "labels": [
    {
      "text": "### [Self Guided Walking Tour San Telmo](…)",
      "atomId": "a-001",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Title heading of the tour article."
    },
    {
      "text": "I'm the type of person that do Excel sheet for each travel itinerary and like to plan ahead everything.",
      "atomId": "a-002",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Personal introduction by the author."
    },
    {
      "text": "That's how I come across for the first time to a Self-Guided Walking Tour post in Edinburgh, and I was like, wow this is amazing.",
      "atomId": "a-003",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Personal anecdote about travel guides."
    },
    {
      "text": "After living 8 years in San Telmo, Buenos Aires I kind of feel ready to do a Guide myself.",
      "atomId": "a-004",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Personal background statement."
    },
    {
      "text": "So here is a 24hs tour to the Center, San Telmo, La Boca and Defensa.",
      "atomId": "a-005",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Overview of the tour itinerary destinations."
    },
    {
      "text": "Be ready to walk around 15km and eat delicious food in the way :) I hope you enjoy it!",
      "atomId": "a-006",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "General tips and introductory remarks."
    },
    {
      "text": "\\* Note: this tour was though to be done not on Sunday.",
      "atomId": "a-007",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Important scheduling note about Sundays."
    },
    {
      "text": "Since San Telmo has a HUGE street fair during Sundays and is a bit crowded, but it can be done anyway maybe we a bit more time.",
      "atomId": "a-008",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Explanation regarding San Telmo on Sundays."
    },
    {
      "text": "\\* *There is a map at the end with all the stops mentioned!*",
      "atomId": "a-009",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Mention of a map at the end."
    },
    {
      "text": "**9am - Teatro Colón**  The itinerary starts from the   Subte station \"Tribunales\".",
      "atomId": "a-010",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Teatro Colón",
          "supportSpan": "Teatro Colón",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 1466,
          "sourceEnd": 1478
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Starting point and first stop of the itinerary."
    },
    {
      "text": "From there you can cross the park   to see the stunning Teatro Colón from outside.",
      "atomId": "a-011",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Teatro Colón",
          "supportSpan": "Teatro Colón",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 1600,
          "sourceEnd": 1612
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs traveler to see Teatro Colón."
    },
    {
      "text": "Then you can walk a few streets to  see the Obelisco and then walkthrough  Av. Roque Saenz Peña directly  to Plaza de Mayo.",
      "atomId": "a-012",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Obelisco",
          "supportSpan": "Obelisco",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 1672,
          "sourceEnd": 1680
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Av. Roque Saenz Peña",
          "supportSpan": "Av. Roque Saenz Peña",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 1703,
          "sourceEnd": 1723
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 1737,
          "sourceEnd": 1750
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs traveler through places to Plaza de Mayo."
    },
    {
      "text": "**10am - Have Breakfast and visit Plaza de Mayo**",
      "atomId": "a-013",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 1795,
          "sourceEnd": 1808
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Heading announcing breakfast and Plaza de Mayo visit."
    },
    {
      "text": "Picture by[@andregrevex](…)",
      "atomId": "a-014",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Photo credit caption."
    },
    {
      "text": "Once you arrive to Plaza de Mayo you can walk through Av. de Mayo (which is really beautiful avenue) at the end of this avenue you can see the Congress building.",
      "atomId": "a-015",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 1920,
          "sourceEnd": 1933
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Av. de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Av. de Mayo",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 1955,
          "sourceEnd": 1966
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Congress building",
          "supportSpan": "Congress building",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 2044,
          "sourceEnd": 2061
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs traveler to Plaza de Mayo, Av. de Mayo, and Congress building."
    },
    {
      "text": "Here I recommend you 2 coffees shop:  **-** the first is the iconic **Café** **Tortoni**, you can enjoy some \"Cafe con medialunas\" this is our typical breakfast.",
      "atomId": "a-016",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Café Tortoni",
          "supportSpan": "Café Tortoni",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 2134,
          "sourceEnd": 2150
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Recommends a coffee shop option."
    },
    {
      "text": "However Tortoni has also nice \"Churros con Chocolate\".",
      "atomId": "a-017",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Additional description of Tortoni."
    },
    {
      "text": "**-**In case Tortoni is too crowded you can walk back to **London City Coffee** where multiple famous writers and iconic figures of Buenos Aires spent time there, such as our writer Cortázar.",
      "atomId": "a-018",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "London City Coffee",
          "supportSpan": "London City Coffee",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 2341,
          "sourceEnd": 2359
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Offers an alternative coffee shop option."
    },
    {
      "text": "Counter of Tortoni Café, Buenos Aires",
      "atomId": "a-019",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Image caption."
    },
    {
      "text": "Then you can walk back through Av. de Mayo and reach Plaza de Mayo again.",
      "atomId": "a-020",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Av. de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Av. de Mayo",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 2568,
          "sourceEnd": 2579
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 2590,
          "sourceEnd": 2603
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs return to Plaza de Mayo."
    },
    {
      "text": "This Plaza is quite important here we have the Casa Rosada, the Cathedral (where the Pope use to give mass) and the Cabildo.",
      "atomId": "a-021",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "This Plaza",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 2611,
          "sourceEnd": 2621,
          "mention": {
            "atomId": "a-020",
            "sourceStart": 2590,
            "sourceEnd": 2603
          }
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Casa Rosada",
          "supportSpan": "Casa Rosada",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 2658,
          "sourceEnd": 2669
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "the Cathedral",
          "supportSpan": "the Cathedral",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 2671,
          "sourceEnd": 2684
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "the Cabildo",
          "supportSpan": "the Cabildo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 2723,
          "sourceEnd": 2734
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Describes sights at Plaza de Mayo."
    },
    {
      "text": "Is a place where most of the manifestation take place since is connected to Congress.",
      "atomId": "a-022",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "General historical and contextual description."
    },
    {
      "text": "[TEXTALT](…)        You can see in the floor of Plaza de Mayo some white Scarfs draw in the floor, this represents the \"Grandmother of Plaza de Mayo\", this are grandmothers you ask until today for their missing grandchildren during the dictatorship.",
      "atomId": "a-023",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "supportSpan": "Plaza de Mayo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 3099,
          "sourceEnd": 3112
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Points out details in Plaza de Mayo."
    },
    {
      "text": "\\*\\* If you want to enter Casa Rosada, you have to book a visit in advance, they are free.",
      "atomId": "a-024",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Practical booking tip for Casa Rosada."
    },
    {
      "text": "Stunning picture by [@aguspiluso](…)",
      "atomId": "a-025",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Photo credit caption."
    },
    {
      "text": "**12 am - Walk through Defensa Street**  Now you are entering San Telmo.",
      "atomId": "a-026",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "San Telmo",
          "supportSpan": "San Telmo",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 3578,
          "sourceEnd": 3587
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Heading indicating next stop and entering San Telmo."
    },
    {
      "text": "Defensa Street is the main street and on Sunday there is a huge street fair that starts from Plaza de Mayo and continues to Plaza Dorrego.",
      "atomId": "a-027",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Defensa Street",
          "supportSpan": "Defensa Street",
