    },
    {
      "text": "- Stop 6: Oldest library in town, **\"La Librería del Avila\"**!, this is the library it has more than 100.000 books and it has been witness of big part of our history.",
      "atomId": "a-031",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "La Librería del Avila",
          "supportSpan": "La Librería del Avila",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 4062,
          "sourceEnd": 4083
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Numbered stop directive for the library."
    },
    {
      "text": "Is used to be call the \"School Library\" because if you look just in front, you can see the prestigious National School of Buenos Aires.",
      "atomId": "a-032",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "National School of Buenos Aires",
          "supportSpan": "National School of Buenos Aires",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 4295,
          "sourceEnd": 4326
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Points out the National School of Buenos Aires."
    },
    {
      "text": "🥩 If you are hungry at this point and want to have launch, I highly recommend having lunch at [Alfonso](…) (in Av. Belgrano 782) cozy place with comfort food and very nice selection of wines and vermouth.",
      "atomId": "a-033",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Alfonso",
          "supportSpan": "Alfonso",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 4427,
          "sourceEnd": 4434
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Recommends a place for lunch."
    },
    {
      "text": "- Stop 7: **Monumento de Mafalda**, this is one of our most loved cartoon characters created by Quino.",
      "atomId": "a-034",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Monumento de Mafalda",
          "supportSpan": "Monumento de Mafalda",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 4598,
          "sourceEnd": 4618
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Numbered stop directive for Monumento de Mafalda."
    },
    {
      "text": "If you never heard of it, it was translated in almost any language and although it looks like a cartoon for kids it talks about world issues about politics and economics that is almost as relevant for adults.",
      "atomId": "a-035",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Provides description and background information about the cartoon."
    },
    {
      "text": "Mafalda use to live in San Telmo exactly in a house in Chile 371 that actually exists, so you can check it out!",
      "atomId": "a-036",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Chile 371",
          "supportSpan": "Chile 371",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 4953,
          "sourceEnd": 4962
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Suggests checking out the fictional character's house."
    },
    {
      "text": "Casa Mínima, San Telmo, Buenos Aires",
      "atomId": "a-037",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Location caption fragment."
    },
    {
      "text": "- Stop 8: **Casa Mínima**, this is known to be the narrowest house in Buenos Aires, not sure if this is true but is cute and the street as well ;)",
      "atomId": "a-038",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Casa Mínima",
          "supportSpan": "Casa Mínima",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 5084,
          "sourceEnd": 5095
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs the traveller to Stop 8 Casa Minima."
    },
    {
      "text": "4 días en Mendoza, Argentina - Itinerario completo día por día de que hacer.",
      "atomId": "a-039",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Irrelevant text or ad."
    },
    {
      "text": "Stop 9: **The San Telmo Market**!!",
      "atomId": "a-040",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "The San Telmo Market",
          "supportSpan": "The San Telmo Market",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 5348,
          "sourceEnd": 5368
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs the traveller to Stop 9."
    },
    {
      "text": "My favorite place in the neighborhood, the oldest market in Buenos Aires and recently  remodeled with a lot of restaurants  (before there were antiquities  and fruit and and vegetable stores).",
      "atomId": "a-041",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Provides description and history of the market."
    },
    {
      "text": "Here there are also a lot of  tourist traps, so be careful.",
      "atomId": "a-042",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Provides tourist advice."
    },
    {
      "text": "Here you have 2 choices, have lunch in the market, or grab something  small and wait to eat some  big meal in La Boca.",
      "atomId": "a-043",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "market",
          "supportSpan": "market",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 5674,
          "sourceEnd": 5680
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "La Boca",
          "supportSpan": "La Boca",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 5741,
          "sourceEnd": 5748
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Offers a choice between having lunch here or later in La Boca."
    },
    {
      "text": "🌭If you go for the small bite, I recommend eating *1 choripan* en **Nuestra Parrilla** (stop 10), is on the outside (over Bolivar street) of the market and not a tourist trap.",
      "atomId": "a-044",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Nuestra Parrilla",
          "supportSpan": "Nuestra Parrilla",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 5832,
          "sourceEnd": 5848
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Recommends a specific optional food stop."
    },
    {
      "text": "🍦Exactly on the opposite side, also on the outside side, in Defensa street you have 2 icecream shops ( if you didn't notice we love ice cream here and we eat a lot of it!)",
      "atomId": "a-045",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Mentions unnamed ice cream shops."
    },
    {
      "text": "☕️If you are craving for some coffee, go to **Coffee Town**, just in the middle of the market, is the best in area!",
      "atomId": "a-046",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Coffee Town",
          "supportSpan": "Coffee Town",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 6163,
          "sourceEnd": 6174
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Recommends an optional coffee spot."
    },
    {
      "text": "🥩 If you for the BIG meal, my favorite restaurant is **Saigón** is kind of Vietnamese - Argentine, I highly recommend trying the Bo Lu Lac (Is meat with rice).",
      "atomId": "a-047",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Saigón",
          "supportSpan": "Saigón",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 6290,
          "sourceEnd": 6296
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Offers one of two restaurant options for the big meal."
    },
    {
      "text": "But I understand if you want to eat asado, so here I would recommend to go to **Desnivel**, is not fancy but you eat really good!",
      "atomId": "a-048",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Desnivel",
          "supportSpan": "Desnivel",
          "role": "ALTERNATIVE",
          "sourceStart": 6475,
          "sourceEnd": 6483
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Offers an alternative restaurant option for asado."
    },
    {
      "text": "Café Rivas, San Telmo, Bueos Aires",
      "atomId": "a-049",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Location caption."
    },
    {
      "text": "**Café Rivas y Galería Solar**    This are two other places you can  visit while you are around.",
      "atomId": "a-050",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Café Rivas y Galería Solar",
          "supportSpan": "Café Rivas y Galería Solar",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 6631,
          "sourceEnd": 6657
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Presents additional places to visit while around."
    },
    {
      "text": "The first  one is Café Rivas, a beautiful café.",
      "atomId": "a-051",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Café Rivas",
          "supportSpan": "Café Rivas",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 6744,
          "sourceEnd": 6754
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Describes the first optional place."
    },
    {
      "text": "Just one block from the San Telmo Market you can find the Galería Solar, this use  to be an old house that is now full of shops.",
      "atomId": "a-052",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Galería Solar",
          "supportSpan": "Galería Solar",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 6835,
          "sourceEnd": 6848
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Describes the second optional place."
    },
    {
      "text": "- Stop 10: Last stop, this is \"**El Patio de los Ezeiza\"**.",
      "atomId": "a-053",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "\"El Patio de los Ezeiza\"",
          "supportSpan": "\"El Patio de los Ezeiza\"",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 6945,
          "sourceEnd": 6967
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs the traveller to the last stop."
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a house that was built around 1876 to house the Ezeiza family, an aristocratic family.",
      "atomId": "a-054",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Provides history of the house."
    },
    {
      "text": "Later, the Ezeiza would leave the house to move to Barrio Norte, like many other upper class families in Buenos Aires during the Yellow Fever Epidemic of 1871.",
      "atomId": "a-055",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Provides historical context."
    },
    {
      "text": "After this is become a school, later a *conventillo* and right now is full of shop so you can just wonder around!",
      "atomId": "a-056",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Provides history and current status."
    },
    {
      "text": "Patio Ezeiza, San Telmo, Buenos Aires, Argentina",
      "atomId": "a-057",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Location caption."
    },
    {
      "text": "**15hs - Go to Caminito en La Boca**",
      "atomId": "a-058",
      "classification": "TRANSFER",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Caminito",
          "supportSpan": "Caminito en La Boca",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 7446,
          "sourceEnd": 7465
        }
      ],
      "transferMode": "BUS",
      "reason": "Heading announcing transfer to the next destination by transport."
    },
    {
      "text": "From \"El Patio de los Ezeiza\" you can take bus 29 to Caminito or take a taxi.",
      "atomId": "a-059",
      "classification": "TRANSFER",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "\"El Patio de los Ezeiza\"",
          "supportSpan": "\"El Patio de los Ezeiza\"",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 7477,
          "sourceEnd": 7499
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Caminito",
          "supportSpan": "Caminito",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 7524,
          "sourceEnd": 7532
        }
      ],
      "transferMode": "BUS",
      "reason": "Describes taking a bus or taxi to the next stop."
    },
    {
      "text": "The taxi should cost about 3usd max (official USD, not the blue USD). You can use Google Maps to get here, it works pretty ok with the buses.",
      "atomId": "a-060",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Navigation tip and pricing details."
    },
    {
      "text": "**CAMINITO, LA BOCA**  An important note here, La Boca is the  neighborhood and is not the type   of neighborhood you want to be at night.",
      "atomId": "a-061",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Safety warning about the neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "text": "However, Caminito is the tourist street   of this neighborhood.",
      "atomId": "a-062",
      "classification": "PASS_BY",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Caminito",
          "supportSpan": "Caminito",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 7888,
          "sourceEnd": 7896
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Mentions the tourist street for orientation."
    },
    {
      "text": "My advice  here is: first, if it is getting darker   rather leave this for another day,  if you choose to go to Caminito, wonder  only where you see tourists, don't go  go beyond this, because as I said,  is not the most friendly  neighborhood out there.",
      "atomId": "a-063",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Safety advice."
    },
    {
      "text": "The tourist part you will notice  is the one with colorful houses  and is about 3-4 blocks.",
      "atomId": "a-064",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Description of the tourist part."
    },
    {
      "text": "You might be hungry by this point, so:   - 🥩 Stop 13: **\"Don Carlos\"** also recommended by Anthony Bourdain in his episode of Parts Unknown in Buenos Aires.",
      "atomId": "a-065",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "\"Don Carlos\"",
          "supportSpan": "\"Don Carlos\"",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 8358,
          "sourceEnd": 8368
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs the traveller to Stop 13 restaurant."
    },
    {
      "text": "A small restaurant run by a family in front of the \"Estadio La Boca\".",
      "atomId": "a-066",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Describes the restaurant without directing a visit."
    },
    {
      "text": "You sit here and the owner will bring you food, no question ask, until you cant not walk anymore and decide to stop eating what it will become one of your best food memories.",
      "atomId": "a-067",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "Describes the restaurant experience."
    },
    {
      "text": "-  Stop 12: After this, you can wander around **Caminito Street**, and maybe check the \"**Fundación Proa**\" sometimes they have interesting exhibitions.",
      "atomId": "a-068",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Caminito Street",
          "supportSpan": "Caminito Street",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 8754,
          "sourceEnd": 8769
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Fundación Proa",
          "supportSpan": "Fundación Proa",
          "role": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 8796,
          "sourceEnd": 8810
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs to Caminito Street and mentions Fundación Proa."
    },
    {
      "text": "**17 / 18hs - Go to Puerto Madero**  Here as well you can take a bus or a taxi for around 3,8usd.",
      "atomId": "a-069",
      "classification": "TRANSFER",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Puerto Madero",
          "supportSpan": "Puerto Madero",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 8882,
          "sourceEnd": 8895
        }
      ],
      "transferMode": "BUS",
      "reason": "Announces transport to Puerto Madero."
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting point here is the **Puente de la Mujer**, this is beautiful day or night.",
      "atomId": "a-070",
      "classification": "ITINERARY_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Puente de la Mujer",
          "supportSpan": "Puente de la Mujer",
          "role": "ITINERARY_STOP",
          "sourceStart": 8993,
          "sourceEnd": 9011
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Directs to Puente de la Mujer."
    },
    {
      "text": "By crossing this bridge you are officially in Puerto Madero, and no wonder that you will see that all streets have suddenly women names.",
      "atomId": "a-071",
      "classification": "PASS_BY",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Puerto Madero",
          "supportSpan": "Puerto Madero",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 9093,
          "sourceEnd": 9106
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Entering Puerto Madero via bridge."
    },
    {
      "text": "Here is there is not much to do more than walking and seeing the contrast of such a new architecture just in from of the oldest neighborhood such as San Telmo.",
      "atomId": "a-072",
      "classification": "NON_ITINERARY",
      "entities": [],
      "reason": "General description and contrast."
    },
    {
      "text": "I like to walk next to the \"Darsena Sur\" and then through Av. Int. Hernan Giralt that is close to an ecological park.",
      "atomId": "a-073",
      "classification": "PASS_BY",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Darsena Sur",
          "supportSpan": "Darsena Sur",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 9379,
          "sourceEnd": 9390
        },
        {
          "sourceName": "Av. Int. Hernan Giralt",
          "supportSpan": "Av. Int. Hernan Giralt",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 9409,
          "sourceEnd": 9431
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Walking past streets and landmarks."
    },
    {
      "text": "If you are hungry at this point I can recommend:  - 🌭 Salad: eat *a choripan* in some of the kiosk over  Av. Int. Hernan Giralt.",
      "atomId": "a-074",
      "classification": "ALTERNATIVE",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Av. Int. Hernan Giralt",
          "supportSpan": "Av. Int. Hernan Giralt",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 9578,
          "sourceEnd": 9600
        }
      ],
      "reason": "Suggests kiosk food option."
    },
    {
      "text": "**20hs - Return home / hotel**    If you return through the marked path, you can see the \"Centro Cultural Kirchner\" that used to be our old Central Post Office.",
      "atomId": "a-075",
      "classification": "TRANSFER",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Centro Cultural Kirchner",
          "supportSpan": "Centro Cultural Kirchner",
          "role": "PASS_BY",
          "sourceStart": 9697,
          "sourceEnd": 9721
        }
      ],
      "transferMode": "UNSPECIFIED",
      "reason": "Return journey heading."
    },
    {
      "text": "They offer guided tours and maybe you can enter to see a part of the building.",
      "atomId": "a-076",
      "classification": "OPTIONAL_STOP",
      "entities": [
        {
          "sourceName": "Centro Cultural Kirchner",
          "supportSpan": "building",
